Let’s be honest - building an in-house finance team sounds great in theory. A finance manager, maybe an assistant, an accountant down the line… until you add up the salaries, software, training, sick leave, holidays, recruitment fees and the time it takes to get everyone up to speed….. Suddenly, it’s not looking quite so appealing.

This is where outsourcing your finance department to [Finance with Flow](http://www.financewithflow.com/contact) could be a smart decision for your business.

## **More Brainpower, Less Cost**

When you work with Finance with Flow, you’re not hiring *one* person – you’re gaining access to a whole outsourced finance department. That means senior-level experience, hands-on support, and specialist knowledge, all for a fraction of the cost of employing a full internal team.

No pension contributions.
No long notice periods.
No expensive recruitment mistakes.

Just the right level of expertise, exactly when you need it.

## **Productivity from the start**

An outsourced finance team is productive from day one. There is no lengthy onboarding, no learning the ropes and you are not reliant on a single individual who may be off sick or annual leave. There will be a whole team who will be able to ensure that your finance function runs smoothly at all times.

Knowing the systems, processes, legal compliance (especially in the construction Industry) means thorough data, timely reporting, proactive problem solving and decisions or advice based on real numbers, not guesswork.

## **Knowledge You Can Lean On**

Finance isn’t just about bookkeeping or ticking compliance boxes. It’s about understanding cash flow, margins, WIP, forecasting, VAT, systems, and strategy – and knowing how they all connect.

## **Scalable, Flexible and Future-Proof**

As your business grows, your finance needs change. Outsourcing means your finance function can scale up or down without disruption.

Instead of constantly restructuring an internal team, you have a flexible finance department that grows with you.

Outsourcing your finance department isn’t about cutting corners – it’s about working smarter!

